## Data Types & Variables

### PIC (Picture) Clause

**Theory:**
PIC defines data type and size. It's one of COBOL's most distinctive features.

**PIC Symbols:**

```
9       Numeric digit (0-9)
X       Alphanumeric character
A       Alphabetic character only
V       Decimal point (implied)
S       Sign (+ or -)
P       Decimal point position
C       Currency symbol
.       Actual decimal point
(n)    Repeat character n times

Examples:
PIC 9(5)          → 5-digit number (00000-99999)
PIC X(30)         → 30-character string
PIC 9(3)V99       → 5 digits with 2 decimal places (XXX.XX)
PIC S9(5)         → Signed number (-99999 to +99999)
PIC 9(5)P(2)      → Number with 2 implied decimal places
PIC A(10)         → Alphabetic only (no numbers)
```

**Complete Data Definitions:**

```cobol
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       
       01 EMPLOYEE-RECORD.
           05 EMP-ID           PIC 9(5).
           05 EMP-NAME         PIC X(30).
           05 EMP-SALARY       PIC 9(7)V99.
           05 EMP-BIRTH-DATE   PIC 9(8).
           05 EMP-ACTIVE       PIC X VALUE 'Y'.
       
       01 CALCULATION-AREA.
           05 COUNTER          PIC 9(5) VALUE ZERO.
           05 SUM-TOTAL        PIC 9(9)V99 VALUE ZERO.
           05 PERCENTAGE       PIC 9V99(4) VALUE ZERO.
       
       01 STRING-VARIABLES.
           05 FIRST-NAME       PIC X(15).
           05 LAST-NAME        PIC X(15).
           05 FULL-NAME        PIC X(31).
       
       01 BOOLEAN-FLAGS.
           05 EOF-FLAG         PIC X VALUE 'N'.
           05 ERROR-FLAG       PIC X VALUE 'N'.
           05 SUCCESS-FLAG     PIC X VALUE 'Y'.
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ PIC clause defines size AND type
- ✅ V is implied decimal (not stored)
- ✅ Default VALUE is spaces (X) or zeros (9)
- ✅ Numeric fields right-justified
- ✅ Alphanumeric fields left-justified

