### Group vs Elementary Items

**Theory:**
Hierarchical data structure with levels (01-49).

```cobol
       01 PERSON-RECORD.                      ← Group item (level 01)
           05 PERSON-NAME.                     ← Group item (level 05)
               10 FIRST-NAME   PIC X(15).      ← Elementary
               10 MIDDLE-NAME  PIC X(15).      ← Elementary
               10 LAST-NAME    PIC X(15).      ← Elementary
           05 PERSON-ADDRESS.                  ← Group item
               10 STREET       PIC X(30).      ← Elementary
               10 CITY         PIC X(20).      ← Elementary
               10 ZIP-CODE     PIC X(10).      ← Elementary
           05 AGE              PIC 9(3).       ← Elementary
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           MOVE "John" TO FIRST-NAME.
           MOVE "Smith" TO LAST-NAME.
           
           DISPLAY PERSON-NAME.        ← Shows entire group
           DISPLAY FIRST-NAME.          ← Shows just first name
           
           MOVE PERSON-RECORD TO OUTPUT-BUFFER.
```

