## Control Structures

### Conditionals (IF, EVALUATE)

**Theory:**
COBOL has explicit, readable conditional statements.

**IF Statement:**

```cobol
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       
       SIMPLE-IF.
           IF AGE >= 18
               DISPLAY "Adult"
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "Minor"
           END-IF.
       
       NESTED-IF.
           IF SALARY > 50000
               IF EXPERIENCE > 5
                   DISPLAY "Senior Developer"
               ELSE
                   DISPLAY "Mid-level Developer"
               END-IF
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "Junior Developer"
           END-IF.
       
       MULTIPLE-CONDITIONS.
           IF AGE >= 18 AND COUNTRY = "USA"
               DISPLAY "Eligible to vote"
           END-IF.
           
           IF STATUS = "ACTIVE" OR STATUS = "PENDING"
               DISPLAY "Account is active"
           END-IF.
           
           IF NOT (AGE < 18)
               DISPLAY "Not a minor"
           END-IF.
```

**EVALUATE (Switch) Statement:**

```cobol
       EVALUATE-GRADE.
           EVALUATE GRADE
               WHEN "A"
                   MOVE 4.0 TO GRADE-POINT
               WHEN "B"
                   MOVE 3.0 TO GRADE-POINT
               WHEN "C"
                   MOVE 2.0 TO GRADE-POINT
               WHEN "D"
                   MOVE 1.0 TO GRADE-POINT
               WHEN "F"
                   MOVE 0.0 TO GRADE-POINT
               WHEN OTHER
                   DISPLAY "Invalid grade"
           END-EVALUATE.
       
       EVALUATE-RANGE.
           EVALUATE TRUE
               WHEN AGE < 13
                   MOVE "Child" TO AGE-CATEGORY
               WHEN AGE < 18
                   MOVE "Teen" TO AGE-CATEGORY
               WHEN AGE < 65
                   MOVE "Adult" TO AGE-CATEGORY
               WHEN OTHER
                   MOVE "Senior" TO AGE-CATEGORY
           END-EVALUATE.
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ IF/ELSE/END-IF is explicit
- ✅ EVALUATE is like switch/case
- ✅ Conditions can be complex with AND/OR/NOT
- ✅ Comparison operators: =, <, >, <=, >=, <>
- ✅ Nested conditions fully supported

