## Procedures & Paragraphs

### Paragraph Organization

**Theory:**
Paragraphs are named blocks of code that can be called with PERFORM.

```cobol
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       
       MAIN-PROCEDURE.
           PERFORM OPEN-FILES.
           PERFORM PROCESS-DATA.
           PERFORM CLOSE-FILES.
           STOP RUN.
       
       OPEN-FILES.
           OPEN INPUT INPUT-FILE.
           OPEN OUTPUT OUTPUT-FILE.
           DISPLAY "Files opened successfully".
       
       PROCESS-DATA.
           PERFORM UNTIL EOF-FLAG = 'Y'
               READ INPUT-FILE
                   AT END
                       MOVE 'Y' TO EOF-FLAG
                   NOT AT END
                       PERFORM PROCESS-RECORD
               END-READ
           END-PERFORM.
       
       PROCESS-RECORD.
           MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(RECORD-NAME) 
               TO RECORD-NAME.
           COMPUTE NEW-SALARY = SALARY * 1.10.
           WRITE OUTPUT-RECORD FROM PROCESSED-DATA.
       
       CLOSE-FILES.
           CLOSE INPUT-FILE.
           CLOSE OUTPUT-FILE.
           DISPLAY "Files closed successfully".
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Paragraph names are identifiers followed by period
- ✅ Paragraphs execute sequentially unless controlled by PERFORM
- ✅ PERFORM transfers control to paragraph
- ✅ Return to next statement after paragraph ends
- ✅ Paragraphs can call other paragraphs

