## Database Operations

### DB2 Integration

**Theory:**
COBOL often works with DB2 (IBM database system) through embedded SQL.

```cobol
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. EMPLOYEE-UPDATE.
       
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 EMP-DATA.
           05 EMP-ID           PIC 9(5).
           05 EMP-NAME         PIC X(30).
           05 EMP-SALARY       PIC 9(7)V99.
       
       01 DB2-STATUS.
           05 SQLCODE          PIC S9(9).
           05 SQLERRM          PIC X(70).
       
       EXEC SQL
           INCLUDE SQLCA
       END-EXEC.
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-PROCEDURE.
           PERFORM CONNECT-DB.
           PERFORM SELECT-EMPLOYEE.
           PERFORM UPDATE-EMPLOYEE.
           PERFORM COMMIT-CHANGES.
           PERFORM DISCONNECT-DB.
           STOP RUN.
       
       CONNECT-DB.
           EXEC SQL
               CONNECT TO EMPDB USER :USERID 
               USING :PASSWORD
           END-EXEC.
           
           IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
               DISPLAY "Connection failed: " SQLERRM
               STOP RUN
           END-IF.
       
       SELECT-EMPLOYEE.
           MOVE 12345 TO EMP-ID.
           
           EXEC SQL
               SELECT NAME, SALARY
               INTO :EMP-NAME, :EMP-SALARY
               FROM EMPLOYEES
               WHERE EMP_ID = :EMP-ID
           END-EXEC.
           
           EVALUATE SQLCODE
               WHEN 0
                   DISPLAY "Found: " EMP-NAME
               WHEN +100
                   DISPLAY "Employee not found"
               WHEN OTHER
                   DISPLAY "Error: " SQLERRM
           END-EVALUATE.
       
       UPDATE-EMPLOYEE.
           COMPUTE EMP-SALARY = EMP-SALARY * 1.10.
           
           EXEC SQL
               UPDATE EMPLOYEES
               SET SALARY = :EMP-SALARY
               WHERE EMP_ID = :EMP-ID
           END-EXEC.
       
       COMMIT-CHANGES.
           EXEC SQL
               COMMIT
           END-EXEC.
       
       DISCONNECT-DB.
           EXEC SQL
               DISCONNECT ALL
           END-EXEC.
```

**SQLCODE Values:**

```
0       ← Success
+100    ← No data found
-1      ← Rollback
-803    ← Duplicate key
-530    ← Foreign key violation
-911    ← Deadlock/timeout
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ EXEC SQL ... END-EXEC for SQL statements
- ✅ Host variables prefixed with :
- ✅ SQLCA for status information
- ✅ Check SQLCODE after each operation
- ✅ COMMIT for transaction control

