## Program Structure & Divisions

### Theory: COBOL Division Hierarchy

**Why Four Divisions?**
COBOL enforces a strict separation of concerns:
```
IDENTIFICATION ─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ WHAT is this program?                                  │
│ Who created it? When?                                  │
│ Purpose and metadata                                   │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

ENVIRONMENT ────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ WHERE will data come from?                             │
│ File definitions, I/O setup                           │
│ External resource configuration                       │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

DATA ───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ WHAT data structures do we use?                        │
│ Variable declarations, record layouts                 │
│ File section, working storage                         │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

PROCEDURE ─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ HOW do we process the data?                           │
│ Logic, calculations, program flow                     │
│ Paragraph definitions                                 │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Practical Example: Complete Program Structure

```cobol
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. STUDENT-GRADE-PROCESSOR.
       AUTHOR. Jane Smith.
       DATE-WRITTEN. 2024-01-15.
       PURPOSE. Process student grades and generate report.
       REMARKS. Reads grades file, calculates averages,
                classifies performance levels.
       
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.
           CLASS PASSING IS 60 THRU 100
           CLASS FAILING IS 0 THRU 59.
       
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT STUDENT-FILE ASSIGN TO 'students.dat'
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL.
           
           SELECT GRADE-FILE ASSIGN TO 'grades.dat'
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               RECORD KEY IS GRADE-ID.
           
           SELECT REPORT-FILE ASSIGN TO 'report.txt'
               ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.
       
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD STUDENT-FILE.
       01 STUDENT-RECORD.
           05 STUDENT-ID           PIC 9(6).
           05 STUDENT-NAME         PIC X(30).
           05 ENROLLMENT-DATE      PIC 9(8).
       
       FD GRADE-FILE.
       01 GRADE-RECORD.
           05 GRADE-ID             PIC 9(6).
           05 SUBJECT               PIC X(20).
           05 GRADE-VALUE          PIC 9(3).
       
       FD REPORT-FILE.
       01 REPORT-LINE              PIC X(80).
       
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-VARIABLES.
           05 WS-EOF               PIC X VALUE 'N'.
           05 WS-TOTAL-GRADE       PIC 9(5) VALUE 0.
           05 WS-GRADE-COUNT       PIC 9(3) VALUE 0.
           05 WS-AVERAGE           PIC 9(3)V99.
           05 WS-PERFORMANCE       PIC X(20).
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-LOGIC.
           OPEN INPUT STUDENT-FILE.
           OPEN OUTPUT REPORT-FILE.
           
           PERFORM PROCESS-GRADES.
           
           CLOSE STUDENT-FILE.
           CLOSE REPORT-FILE.
           STOP RUN.
       
       PROCESS-GRADES.
           PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = 'Y'
               READ STUDENT-FILE
                   AT END
                       MOVE 'Y' TO WS-EOF
                   NOT AT END
                       PERFORM CALCULATE-AVERAGE
                       PERFORM WRITE-REPORT
               END-READ
           END-PERFORM.
       
       CALCULATE-AVERAGE.
           DIVIDE WS-TOTAL-GRADE BY WS-GRADE-COUNT
               GIVING WS-AVERAGE
               ROUNDED.
           
           EVALUATE TRUE
               WHEN WS-AVERAGE >= 90
                   MOVE "Excellent" TO WS-PERFORMANCE
               WHEN WS-AVERAGE >= 80
                   MOVE "Good" TO WS-PERFORMANCE
               WHEN WS-AVERAGE >= 70
                   MOVE "Fair" TO WS-PERFORMANCE
               WHEN WS-AVERAGE >= 60
                   MOVE "Pass" TO WS-PERFORMANCE
               WHEN OTHER
                   MOVE "Fail" TO WS-PERFORMANCE
           END-EVALUATE.
       
       WRITE-REPORT.
           STRING
               "Student: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               STUDENT-NAME DELIMITED BY SPACE
               " | Average: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               WS-AVERAGE DELIMITED BY SIZE
               " | Status: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               WS-PERFORMANCE DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO REPORT-LINE
           END-STRING.
           WRITE REPORT-LINE.
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Each division has specific purpose
- ✅ Divisions appear in fixed order
- ✅ File-CONTROL links logical names to physical files
- ✅ Working-STORAGE holds temporary variables
- ✅ Procedure division contains all logic

