## Procedures & Paragraphs

### Theory: Code Organization with Paragraphs

**Paragraph Structure:**
```
PARAGRAPH-NAME.
    *> Code here
    statement1.
    statement2.
    statement3.
```

### Practical Examples: Paragraph Organization

```cobol
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-PROCEDURE.
           *> Main entry point
           PERFORM INITIALIZE-SYSTEM.
           PERFORM PROCESS-DATA.
           PERFORM GENERATE-REPORTS.
           PERFORM CLEANUP.
           STOP RUN.
       
       INITIALIZE-SYSTEM.
           *> Set up initial state
           MOVE 0 TO TOTAL-RECORDS.
           MOVE 'N' TO EOF-FLAG.
           MOVE SPACES TO ERROR-MESSAGE.
           OPEN INPUT INPUT-FILE.
           OPEN OUTPUT OUTPUT-FILE.
       
       PROCESS-DATA.
           *> Main processing loop
           PERFORM UNTIL EOF-FLAG = 'Y'
               READ INPUT-FILE
                   AT END
                       MOVE 'Y' TO EOF-FLAG
                   NOT AT END
                       PERFORM VALIDATE-RECORD
                       IF RECORD-VALID = 'Y'
                           PERFORM CALCULATE
                           PERFORM WRITE-OUTPUT
                       END-IF
               END-READ
           END-PERFORM.
       
       VALIDATE-RECORD.
           *> Check if record is valid
           MOVE 'Y' TO RECORD-VALID.
           
           IF FIELD-A IS NUMERIC
               CONTINUE
           ELSE
               MOVE 'N' TO RECORD-VALID
           END-IF.
           
           IF FIELD-B >= 0 AND FIELD-B <= 100
               CONTINUE
           ELSE
               MOVE 'N' TO RECORD-VALID
           END-IF.
       
       CALCULATE.
           *> Perform calculations
           COMPUTE RESULT = FIELD-A * FIELD-B / 100.
           ADD 1 TO TOTAL-RECORDS.
       
       WRITE-OUTPUT.
           *> Write processed record
           STRING
               FIELD-A DELIMITED BY SIZE
               " | " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               FIELD-B DELIMITED BY SIZE
               " | " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               RESULT DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO OUTPUT-RECORD
           END-STRING.
           WRITE OUTPUT-RECORD.
       
       GENERATE-REPORTS.
           *> Create summary reports
           PERFORM WRITE-HEADER.
           PERFORM WRITE-SUMMARY.
           PERFORM WRITE-FOOTER.
       
       WRITE-HEADER.
           MOVE "=== REPORT ===" TO REPORT-LINE.
           WRITE REPORT-LINE.
       
       WRITE-SUMMARY.
           STRING
               "Total Records: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               TOTAL-RECORDS DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO REPORT-LINE
           END-STRING.
           WRITE REPORT-LINE.
       
       WRITE-FOOTER.
           MOVE "=== END ===" TO REPORT-LINE.
           WRITE REPORT-LINE.
       
       CLEANUP.
           *> Close files and cleanup
           CLOSE INPUT-FILE.
           CLOSE OUTPUT-FILE.
           DISPLAY "Processing complete".
```

**Paragraph Best Practices:**
```
✓ Single responsibility principle
✓ Meaningful names
✓ 20-50 lines max
✓ Clear purpose
✓ Logical grouping
✓ No complex nesting
```

