## File Handling

### Theory: File Organization Types

```
SEQUENTIAL FILES:
├─ Records stored one after another
├─ Read from start to end
├─ Cannot skip records
├─ Fast for batch processing
├─ Example: transaction logs

INDEXED (ISAM) FILES:
├─ Key-based access
├─ Fast random access
├─ Can also read sequentially
├─ Example: employee database

RELATIVE FILES:
├─ Access by position/record number
├─ Less common
├─ Example: fixed-size record files
```

### Practical Examples: File Operations

```cobol
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT CUSTOMER-FILE ASSIGN TO 'customers.dat'
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL.
           
           SELECT ACCOUNT-FILE ASSIGN TO 'accounts.dat'
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               RECORD KEY IS ACCOUNT-NUMBER
               ALTERNATE RECORD KEY IS CUSTOMER-ID.
           
           SELECT REPORT-FILE ASSIGN TO 'report.txt'
               ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.
       
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD CUSTOMER-FILE.
       01 CUSTOMER-RECORD.
           05 CUSTOMER-ID          PIC 9(7).
           05 CUSTOMER-NAME        PIC X(40).
           05 CUSTOMER-EMAIL       PIC X(50).
       
       FD ACCOUNT-FILE.
       01 ACCOUNT-RECORD.
           05 ACCOUNT-NUMBER       PIC 9(12).
           05 CUSTOMER-ID          PIC 9(7).
           05 ACCOUNT-BALANCE      PIC 9(9)V99.
           05 LAST-TRANSACTION     PIC 9(8).
       
       FD REPORT-FILE.
       01 REPORT-LINE              PIC X(132).
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       
       SEQUENTIAL-FILE-PROCESSING.
           *> Read entire sequential file
           OPEN INPUT CUSTOMER-FILE.
           PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = 'Y'
               READ CUSTOMER-FILE
                   AT END
                       MOVE 'Y' TO WS-EOF
                   NOT AT END
                       PERFORM PROCESS-CUSTOMER
               END-READ
           END-PERFORM.
           CLOSE CUSTOMER-FILE.
       
       INDEXED-FILE-RANDOM-ACCESS.
           *> Direct access using key
           OPEN INPUT ACCOUNT-FILE.
           
           MOVE 123456789012 TO ACCOUNT-NUMBER.
           
           READ ACCOUNT-FILE
               INVALID KEY
                   DISPLAY "Account not found"
               NOT INVALID KEY
                   DISPLAY "Balance: " ACCOUNT-BALANCE
           END-READ.
           
           CLOSE ACCOUNT-FILE.
       
       INDEXED-FILE-SEQUENTIAL-ACCESS.
           *> Read indexed file in sequence
           OPEN INPUT ACCOUNT-FILE.
           
           START ACCOUNT-FILE
               KEY IS >= ACCOUNT-NUMBER
               INVALID KEY
                   DISPLAY "No accounts found"
           END-START.
           
           PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = 'Y'
               READ ACCOUNT-FILE NEXT
                   AT END
                       MOVE 'Y' TO WS-EOF
                   NOT AT END
                       PERFORM PROCESS-ACCOUNT
               END-READ
           END-PERFORM.
           
           CLOSE ACCOUNT-FILE.
       
       WRITE-OUTPUT-FILE.
           OPEN OUTPUT REPORT-FILE.
           
           MOVE "Customer Report" TO REPORT-LINE.
           WRITE REPORT-LINE.
           
           MOVE "=" TO REPORT-LINE.
           WRITE REPORT-LINE.
           
           PERFORM VARYING IDX FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL IDX > CUSTOMER-COUNT
               STRING
                   "Customer: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
                   CUSTOMER-NAME DELIMITED BY SPACE
                   INTO REPORT-LINE
               END-STRING
               WRITE REPORT-LINE
           END-PERFORM.
           
           CLOSE REPORT-FILE.
       
       FILE-STATUS-HANDLING.
           *> Advanced file status checking
           SELECT SECURE-FILE ASSIGN TO 'secure.dat'
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS-CODE.
           
           01 FILE-STATUS-CODE     PIC XX.
           
           OPEN INPUT SECURE-FILE.
           
           IF FILE-STATUS-CODE NOT = "00"
               EVALUATE FILE-STATUS-CODE
                   WHEN "10"
                       DISPLAY "End of file"
                   WHEN "35"
                       DISPLAY "File not found"
                   WHEN "37"
                       DISPLAY "File access denied"
                   WHEN OTHER
                       DISPLAY "File error: " FILE-STATUS-CODE
               END-EVALUATE
           END-IF.
           
           CLOSE SECURE-FILE.
```

**File Status Codes:**
```
00 = Successful operation
10 = End of file
20 = Invalid key / record not found
21 = Key is invalid
22 = Duplicate key
23 = Record out of sequence
24 = Boundary violation
30 = I/O fatal error
34 = Record size exceeds file limits
35 = File not found
36 = File already exists
37 = File access denied
38 = File locked by another user
39 = File already open
45 = Unsupported operation
```

