## String Operations

### Theory: String Manipulation in COBOL

```
STRING   - Concatenate multiple strings
UNSTRING - Split string into parts
INSPECT  - Find/replace characters
MOVE     - Copy strings with padding
ACCEPT   - Read from input
DISPLAY  - Write to output
```

### Practical Examples: String Operations

```cobol
       STRING-OPERATIONS.
       
       SIMPLE-STRING-CONCAT.
           MOVE "Hello" TO STR-A.
           MOVE "World" TO STR-B.
           STRING
               STR-A DELIMITED BY SIZE
               " " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               STR-B DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO FULL-STRING
           END-STRING.
           *> FULL-STRING = "Hello World"
       
       STRING-WITH-DELIMITER.
           MOVE "John" TO FIRST-NAME.
           MOVE "Smith" TO LAST-NAME.
           STRING
               FIRST-NAME DELIMITED BY SPACE
               ", " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               LAST-NAME DELIMITED BY SPACE
               INTO FULL-NAME
           END-STRING.
           *> FULL-NAME = "John, Smith"
       
       UNSTRING-OPERATION.
           MOVE "John,Smith,john@example.com" 
               TO INPUT-STRING.
           
           UNSTRING INPUT-STRING
               DELIMITED BY ","
               INTO FNAME, LNAME, EMAIL
               END-UNSTRING.
           *> FNAME = "John"
           *> LNAME = "Smith"
           *> EMAIL = "john@example.com"
       
       UNSTRING-MULTIPLE-DELIMITERS.
           MOVE "Date: 2024-01-15; Time: 14:30:25"
               TO INPUT-DATA.
           
           UNSTRING INPUT-DATA
               DELIMITED BY ":" OR "-" OR ";"
               INTO LABEL1, VALUE1, 
                    LABEL2, VALUE2
               END-UNSTRING.
       
       INSPECT-FIND-REPLACE.
           MOVE "Hello World World" TO TEXT-VAR.
           
           *> Count occurrences
           INSPECT TEXT-VAR TALLYING OCCUR-COUNT
               FOR ALL "World".
           *> OCCUR-COUNT = 2
           
           *> Replace character
           INSPECT TEXT-VAR REPLACING ALL "o"
               BY "0".
           *> TEXT-VAR = "Hell0 W0rld W0rld"
           
           *> Replace first occurrence
           INSPECT TEXT-VAR REPLACING FIRST "Hello"
               BY "Hi".
           *> TEXT-VAR = "Hi World World"
       
       STRING-LENGTH-OPERATIONS.
           MOVE "Hello World" TO TEXT-VAR.
           
           MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(TEXT-VAR)
               TO TEXT-LENGTH.
           *> TEXT-LENGTH = 11
           
           MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(TEXT-VAR))
               TO TRIMMED-LENGTH.
           *> TRIMMED-LENGTH = 11
       
       CASE-CONVERSION.
           MOVE "Hello World" TO ORIGINAL-TEXT.
           
           *> Convert to uppercase
           MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(ORIGINAL-TEXT)
               TO UPPER-TEXT.
           *> UPPER-TEXT = "HELLO WORLD"
           
           *> Convert to lowercase
           MOVE FUNCTION LOWER-CASE(ORIGINAL-TEXT)
               TO LOWER-TEXT.
           *> LOWER-TEXT = "hello world"
       
       STRING-TRIMMING.
           MOVE "  Hello  " TO PADDED-TEXT.
           
           *> Trim both sides
           MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(PADDED-TEXT)
               TO TRIMMED-TEXT.
           *> TRIMMED-TEXT = "Hello"
           
           *> Trim leading spaces only
           MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(PADDED-TEXT 
               LEADING) TO TRIM-LEADING.
           *> TRIM-LEADING = "Hello  "
           
           *> Trim trailing spaces only
           MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(PADDED-TEXT 
               TRAILING) TO TRIM-TRAILING.
           *> TRIM-TRAILING = "  Hello"
       
       STRING-SUBSTRING.
           MOVE "Hello World" TO ORIGINAL-TEXT.
           
           *> Extract substring
           *> MID (starting position, length)
           MOVE FUNCTION MID(ORIGINAL-TEXT, 7, 5)
               TO SUBSTRING.
           *> SUBSTRING = "World"
       
       STRING-SEARCH.
           MOVE "hello world hello" TO SEARCH-TEXT.
           
           *> Find position
           MOVE FUNCTION POSITION("world" IN SEARCH-TEXT)
               TO POSITION-VALUE.
           *> POSITION-VALUE = 7
```

