## Arrays & Tables

### Theory: Data Structures in COBOL

**COBOL doesn't have arrays like other languages, but uses OCCURS:**
```
OCCURS - Repeats data structure multiple times
Used for:
├─ Arrays of values
├─ Tables of records
├─ Multi-dimensional arrays
└─ Dynamic arrays (DEPENDING ON)
```

### Practical Examples: Arrays & Tables

```cobol
       ARRAYS-AND-TABLES.
       
       01 SIMPLE-ARRAY.
           05 NUMBERS               PIC 9(3) OCCURS 10.
               *> Array of 10 numbers
               *> Access: NUMBERS(1), NUMBERS(2)...
       
       01 ARRAY-WITH-INDEX.
           05 NAMES                 PIC X(30) OCCURS 100.
               *> Array of 100 names
           
           05 NAME-INDEX            PIC 999.
       
       01 STRUCTURED-ARRAY.
           05 EMPLOYEE-TABLE OCCURS 50 TIMES.
               10 EMP-ID            PIC 9(5).
               10 EMP-NAME          PIC X(30).
               10 EMP-SALARY        PIC 9(7)V99.
               10 EMP-DEPARTMENT    PIC X(20).
               *> 50 employee records
       
       01 MULTI-DIMENSIONAL-ARRAY.
           05 MATRIX OCCURS 5 TIMES.
               10 ROW-DATA OCCURS 10 TIMES.
                   15 MATRIX-VALUE  PIC 9(3).
               *> 5x10 matrix
               *> Access: MATRIX-VALUE(row, col)
       
       01 DYNAMIC-ARRAY.
           05 ARRAY-SIZE            PIC 9(3) VALUE 0.
           05 DYNAMIC-DATA OCCURS 1000 TIMES
               DEPENDING ON ARRAY-SIZE.
               10 ITEM-CODE         PIC X(10).
               10 ITEM-VALUE        PIC 9(5)V99.
               *> Only use first ARRAY-SIZE elements
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       
       POPULATE-ARRAY.
           PERFORM VARYING IDX FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL IDX > 10
               MOVE IDX TO NUMBERS(IDX)
           END-PERFORM.
       
       PROCESS-EMPLOYEE-TABLE.
           PERFORM VARYING EMP-INDEX FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL EMP-INDEX > 50
               IF EMP-SALARY(EMP-INDEX) > 75000
                   ADD 1 TO HIGH-EARNER-COUNT
               END-IF
           END-PERFORM.
       
       MATRIX-OPERATIONS.
           *> Populate matrix
           PERFORM VARYING ROW FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL ROW > 5
               PERFORM VARYING COL FROM 1 BY 1
                   UNTIL COL > 10
                   COMPUTE MATRIX-VALUE(ROW, COL) =
                       ROW * COL
               END-PERFORM
           END-PERFORM.
           
           *> Print matrix
           PERFORM VARYING ROW FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL ROW > 5
               MOVE SPACES TO OUTPUT-LINE
               PERFORM VARYING COL FROM 1 BY 1
                   UNTIL COL > 10
                   STRING
                       OUTPUT-LINE DELIMITED BY SIZE
                       MATRIX-VALUE(ROW, COL) 
                           DELIMITED BY SIZE
                       " " DELIMITED BY SIZE
                       INTO OUTPUT-LINE
                   END-STRING
               END-PERFORM
               WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM OUTPUT-LINE
           END-PERFORM.
       
       SEARCH-IN-ARRAY.
           *> Linear search
           MOVE 'N' TO FOUND-FLAG.
           PERFORM VARYING IDX FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL IDX > 100 OR FOUND-FLAG = 'Y'
               IF NAMES(IDX) = SEARCH-NAME
                   MOVE 'Y' TO FOUND-FLAG
                   MOVE IDX TO FOUND-POSITION
               END-IF
           END-PERFORM.
       
       BINARY-SEARCH.
           *> Assumes array is sorted
           MOVE 1 TO LOW-INDEX.
           MOVE 100 TO HIGH-INDEX.
           MOVE 0 TO FOUND-POSITION.
           
           PERFORM UNTIL LOW-INDEX > HIGH-INDEX
               COMPUTE MID-INDEX = 
                   (LOW-INDEX + HIGH-INDEX) / 2
               
               IF NAMES(MID-INDEX) = SEARCH-NAME
                   MOVE MID-INDEX TO FOUND-POSITION
                   MOVE 101 TO LOW-INDEX
               ELSE IF NAMES(MID-INDEX) < SEARCH-NAME
                   COMPUTE LOW-INDEX = MID-INDEX + 1
               ELSE
                   COMPUTE HIGH-INDEX = MID-INDEX - 1
               END-IF
               END-IF
           END-PERFORM.
```

