```

### Practical Examples: CALL & Subroutines

```cobol
       *> MAIN PROGRAM
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. MAIN-PROGRAM.
       
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-INPUT              PIC 9(5).
       01 WS-OUTPUT             PIC 9(5).
       01 WS-STATUS             PIC 9.
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       
       CALL-SUBROUTINE.
           MOVE 100 TO WS-INPUT.
           
           CALL "SQUARE-CALC" USING BY VALUE WS-INPUT
               RETURNING WS-OUTPUT
               GIVING WS-STATUS.
           
           IF WS-STATUS = 0
               DISPLAY "Result: " WS-OUTPUT
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "Error"
           END-IF.
           
           STOP RUN.
       
       
       *> ======================================
       *> SUBROUTINE PROGRAM
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. SQUARE-CALC.
       
       DATA DIVISION.
       LINKAGE SECTION.
       01 LS-INPUT              PIC 9(5).
       01 LS-OUTPUT             PIC 9(5).
       
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-RESULT             PIC 9(9).
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LS-INPUT
           RETURNING LS-OUTPUT.
       
       CALCULATE-SQUARE.
           COMPUTE WS-RESULT = LS-INPUT * LS-INPUT.
           
           IF WS-RESULT <= 99999
               MOVE WS-RESULT TO LS-OUTPUT
           ELSE
               MOVE 0 TO LS-OUTPUT
           END-IF.
           
           GOBACK.
```

**BY VALUE vs BY REFERENCE:**
```cobol
       BY-VALUE-EXAMPLE.
           MOVE 100 TO ORIGINAL-VALUE.
           CALL "MODIFY-VALUE" USING BY VALUE ORIGINAL-VALUE.
           *> ORIGINAL-VALUE still = 100 (unchanged)
       
       BY-REFERENCE-EXAMPLE.
           MOVE 100 TO ORIGINAL-VALUE.
           CALL "MODIFY-VALUE" USING BY REFERENCE ORIGINAL-VALUE.
           *> ORIGINAL-VALUE may be changed by subroutine
```

