## Database Operations

### Theory: SQL in COBOL

```
EMBEDDED SQL:
├─ SELECT - Retrieve data
├─ INSERT - Add new records
├─ UPDATE - Modify records
├─ DELETE - Remove records
└─ COMMIT/ROLLBACK - Transaction control
```

### Practical Examples: SQL Operations

```cobol
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. DATABASE-OPERATIONS.
       
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-VARIABLES.
           05 EMP-ID                PIC 9(7).
           05 EMP-NAME              PIC X(40).
           05 SALARY                PIC 9(7)V99.
           05 SQL-STATUS            PIC S9(9) COMP.
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       
       SELECT-OPERATION.
           MOVE 12345 TO EMP-ID.
           
           EXEC SQL
               SELECT EMPNAME, SALARY INTO :EMP-NAME, :SALARY
               FROM EMPLOYEES
               WHERE EMPID = :EMP-ID
           END-EXEC.
           
           IF SQLCODE = 0
               DISPLAY "Found: " EMP-NAME " - $" SALARY
           ELSE IF SQLCODE = 100
               DISPLAY "Employee not found"
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "Database error: " SQLCODE
           END-IF
           END-IF.
       
       INSERT-OPERATION.
           MOVE 99999 TO EMP-ID.
           MOVE "John Smith" TO EMP-NAME.
           MOVE 50000.00 TO SALARY.
           
           EXEC SQL
               INSERT INTO EMPLOYEES 
               (EMPID, EMPNAME, SALARY)
               VALUES (:EMP-ID, :EMP-NAME, :SALARY)
           END-EXEC.
           
           IF SQLCODE = 0
               DISPLAY "Record inserted successfully"
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "Insert failed: " SQLCODE
           END-IF.
       
       UPDATE-OPERATION.
           MOVE 12345 TO EMP-ID.
           MOVE 55000.00 TO SALARY.
           
           EXEC SQL
               UPDATE EMPLOYEES
               SET SALARY = :SALARY
               WHERE EMPID = :EMP-ID
           END-EXEC.
           
           IF SQLCODE = 0
               DISPLAY "Record updated"
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "Update failed: " SQLCODE
           END-IF.
       
       DELETE-OPERATION.
           MOVE 12345 TO EMP-ID.
           
           EXEC SQL
               DELETE FROM EMPLOYEES
               WHERE EMPID = :EMP-ID
           END-EXEC.
           
           IF SQLCODE = 0
               DISPLAY "Record deleted"
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "Delete failed: " SQLCODE
           END-IF.
       
       CURSOR-OPERATIONS.
           EXEC SQL
               DECLARE EMP-CURSOR CURSOR FOR
               SELECT EMPID, EMPNAME, SALARY
               FROM EMPLOYEES
               WHERE SALARY > 50000
               ORDER BY SALARY DESC
           END-EXEC.
           
           EXEC SQL OPEN EMP-CURSOR END-EXEC.
           
           PERFORM UNTIL SQLCODE NOT = 0
               EXEC SQL
                   FETCH EMP-CURSOR INTO 
                   :EMP-ID, :EMP-NAME, :SALARY
               END-EXEC
               
               IF SQLCODE = 0
                   DISPLAY EMP-ID " " EMP-NAME 
                       " " SALARY
               END-IF
           END-PERFORM.
           
           EXEC SQL CLOSE EMP-CURSOR END-EXEC.
       
       TRANSACTION-CONTROL.
           EXEC SQL BEGIN WORK END-EXEC.
           
           PERFORM INSERT-OPERATION.
           PERFORM UPDATE-OPERATION.
           
           IF SQLCODE = 0
               EXEC SQL COMMIT WORK END-EXEC
               DISPLAY "Transaction committed"
           ELSE
               EXEC SQL ROLLBACK WORK END-EXEC
               DISPLAY "Transaction rolled back"
           END-IF.
```

**Common SQLCODE Values:**
```
0     = Success
100   = No more data / Not found
-1    = Rollback
-803  = Duplicate key
-530  = Foreign key violation
-911  = Deadlock / Timeout
-913  = Deadlock or resource timeout
```

