## Error Handling & Debugging

### Theory: Error Handling Strategies

```
ERROR HANDLING LEVELS:

1. INPUT VALIDATION
   └─ Check data before processing

2. FILE STATUS CHECKING
   └─ Check file operations

3. SQL CODE CHECKING
   └─ Check database operations

4. DIVISION BY ZERO
   └─ Check arithmetic operations

5. BOUNDS CHECKING
   └─ Check array access

6. TRANSACTION ROLLBACK
   └─ Undo failed operations
```

### Practical Examples: Error Handling

```cobol
       ERROR-HANDLING-STRATEGIES.
       
       01 ERROR-FLAGS.
           05 ERROR-OCCURRED        PIC X VALUE 'N'.
           05 ERROR-MESSAGE         PIC X(100).
           05 ERROR-CODE            PIC 9(5).
       
       COMPREHENSIVE-ERROR-HANDLING.
           
           PERFORM VALIDATE-INPUT.
           IF ERROR-OCCURRED = 'Y'
               PERFORM LOG-ERROR
               PERFORM RECOVERY-PROCEDURE
               GOBACK
           END-IF.
           
           PERFORM PROCESS-FILE.
           IF ERROR-OCCURRED = 'Y'
               PERFORM CLEANUP
               GOBACK
           END-IF.
       
       VALIDATE-INPUT.
           MOVE 'N' TO ERROR-OCCURRED.
           
           IF INPUT-VALUE NOT NUMERIC
               MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
               MOVE "Invalid numeric input" 
                   TO ERROR-MESSAGE
               MOVE 1001 TO ERROR-CODE
               EXIT PARAGRAPH
           END-IF.
           
           IF INPUT-VALUE < 0 OR INPUT-VALUE > 999999
               MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
               MOVE "Value out of range" 
                   TO ERROR-MESSAGE
               MOVE 1002 TO ERROR-CODE
               EXIT PARAGRAPH
           END-IF.
           
           IF INPUT-LENGTH = 0
               MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
               MOVE "Empty input not allowed" 
                   TO ERROR-MESSAGE
               MOVE 1003 TO ERROR-CODE
               EXIT PARAGRAPH
           END-IF.
       
       FILE-ERROR-HANDLING.
           SELECT INPUT-FILE ASSIGN TO 'data.txt'
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS-CODE.
           
           01 FILE-STATUS-CODE     PIC XX.
           
           OPEN INPUT INPUT-FILE.
           
           EVALUATE FILE-STATUS-CODE
               WHEN "00"
                   CONTINUE
               WHEN "35"
                   MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
                   MOVE "File not found" TO ERROR-MESSAGE
                   MOVE 2001 TO ERROR-CODE
               WHEN "37"
                   MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
                   MOVE "Permission denied" TO ERROR-MESSAGE
                   MOVE 2002 TO ERROR-CODE
               WHEN "39"
                   MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
                   MOVE "File already open" TO ERROR-MESSAGE
                   MOVE 2003 TO ERROR-CODE
               WHEN OTHER
                   MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
                   MOVE "File error" TO ERROR-MESSAGE
                   MOVE 2999 TO ERROR-CODE
           END-EVALUATE.
       
       DIVISION-BY-ZERO-CHECK.
           IF DENOMINATOR = 0
               MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
               MOVE "Division by zero" TO ERROR-MESSAGE
               MOVE 3001 TO ERROR-CODE
               MOVE 0 TO RESULT
               EXIT PARAGRAPH
           END-IF.
           
           DIVIDE NUMERATOR BY DENOMINATOR
               GIVING RESULT ROUNDED
           END-DIVIDE.
       
       ARRAY-BOUNDS-CHECK.
           IF ARRAY-INDEX < 1 OR ARRAY-INDEX > 100
               MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
               MOVE "Array index out of bounds" 
                   TO ERROR-MESSAGE
               MOVE 4001 TO ERROR-CODE
               EXIT PARAGRAPH
           END-IF.
           
           MOVE ARRAY-DATA(ARRAY-INDEX) TO RESULT.
       
       TRANSACTION-ERROR-HANDLING.
           EXEC SQL BEGIN WORK END-EXEC.
           
           PERFORM INSERT-OPERATION.
           IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
               MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
               STRING "Database error: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
                   SQLCODE DELIMITED BY SIZE
                   INTO ERROR-MESSAGE
               EXEC SQL ROLLBACK WORK END-EXEC
               MOVE 5001 TO ERROR-CODE
               EXIT PARAGRAPH
           END-IF.
           
           PERFORM UPDATE-OPERATION.
           IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
               MOVE 'Y' TO ERROR-OCCURRED
               STRING "Update failed: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
                   SQLCODE DELIMITED BY SIZE
                   INTO ERROR-MESSAGE
               EXEC SQL ROLLBACK WORK END-EXEC
               MOVE 5002 TO ERROR-CODE
               EXIT PARAGRAPH
           END-IF.
           
           EXEC SQL COMMIT WORK END-EXEC.
       
       LOG-ERROR.
           OPEN APPEND ERROR-LOG-FILE.
           
           MOVE SPACES TO ERROR-LOG-RECORD.
           STRING
               "Timestamp: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               CURRENT-DATE DELIMITED BY SIZE
               " | Error Code: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               ERROR-CODE DELIMITED BY SIZE
               " | Message: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
               ERROR-MESSAGE DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO ERROR-LOG-RECORD
           END-STRING.
           
           WRITE ERROR-LOG-RECORD.
           CLOSE ERROR-LOG-FILE.
       
       RECOVERY-PROCEDURE.
           *> Cleanup and restore state
           IF INPUT-FILE IS OPEN
               CLOSE INPUT-FILE
           END-IF.
           
           IF OUTPUT-FILE IS OPEN
               CLOSE OUTPUT-FILE
           END-IF.
           
           IF DATABASE-CURSOR IS OPEN
               EXEC SQL CLOSE DATABASE-CURSOR END-EXEC
           END-IF.
           
           DISPLAY "Error recovery completed".
```

