### Q5: What are all the COBOL data types and when to use each?

**Answer:**

```cobol
       01 NUMERIC-TYPES.
           05 SIMPLE-INTEGER        PIC 9(5).
               *> Range: 0 to 99,999
               *> Use: Counts, IDs, simple numbers
           
           05 SIGNED-INTEGER        PIC S9(5).
               *> Range: -99,999 to +99,999
               *> Use: Amounts, debits/credits
           
           05 DECIMAL-IMPLICIT      PIC 9(5)V99.
               *> Range: 0 to 99,999.99
               *> Storage: 3 bytes (COMP-3)
               *> Use: Internal calculations
           
           05 DECIMAL-EXPLICIT      PIC 9(5).99.
               *> Range: 0 to 99,999.99
               *> Storage: 4 bytes
               *> Use: Output, file storage
           
           05 LARGE-NUMBER          PIC 9(18).
               *> Range: 0 to 999...999 (18 digits)
               *> Use: Large calculations
           
           05 ZERO-SUPPRESSED       PIC Z(5)9.
               *> Suppresses leading zeros
               *> Value: 00123 displays as "   123"
               *> Use: Report formatting
           
           05 CURRENCY-FORMAT       PIC $9(5).99.
               *> Value: 1234.56 displays as "$1234.56"
               *> Use: Currency display
       
       01 ALPHANUMERIC-TYPES.
           05 FIXED-TEXT            PIC X(30).
               *> Fixed 30 characters
               *> Use: Names, codes, descriptions
           
           05 VARIABLE-TEXT         PIC X(50).
               *> Up to 50 characters
               *> Use: Comments, addresses
       
       01 COMPRESSED-TYPES.
           05 BINARY-COMP           PIC 9(4) COMP.
               *> Binary format
               *> Storage: 2 bytes (vs 4 normal)
               *> Use: Calculations, counters
           
           05 PACKED-COMP3          PIC 9(5) COMP-3.
               *> Packed decimal
               *> Storage: 3 bytes (vs 5 normal)
               *> Use: File storage, calculations
           
           05 NATIVE-COMP5          PIC 9(9) COMP-5.
               *> Native binary
               *> Storage: 4 bytes (vs 9 normal)
               *> Use: System calculations
       
       01 SPECIAL-TYPES.
           05 DATE-VALUE            PIC 9(8).
               *> Format: YYYYMMDD (20240115)
               *> Use: Dates
           
           05 TIME-VALUE            PIC 9(6).
               *> Format: HHMMSS (143025)
               *> Use: Times
           
