### Q6: What's the purpose of the REDEFINES clause?

**Answer:**

```cobol
       01 EMPLOYEE-RECORD.
           05 EMP-FULL-NAME        PIC X(40).
           05 EMP-BIRTH-DATE       PIC 9(8).
           05 EMP-SALARY           PIC 9(7)V99.
       
       01 EMPLOYEE-RECORD-VIEW REDEFINES EMPLOYEE-RECORD.
           *> Same storage space, different structure
           05 EMP-FIRST-NAME       PIC X(20).
           05 EMP-LAST-NAME        PIC X(20).
           05 EMP-AGE               PIC 9(3).
           05 EMP-BIRTH-YEAR       PIC 9(4).
           05 EMP-BIRTH-MONTH      PIC 9(2).
           05 EMP-BIRTH-DAY        PIC 9(2).
           05 EMP-ANNUAL           PIC 9(9).
```

**REDEFINES Purpose:**

```
1. VIEW SAME DATA DIFFERENTLY
   ├─ Same physical memory
   ├─ Different logical structure
   └─ Useful for data conversion

2. SAVE STORAGE SPACE
   ├─ Reuse memory for different purposes
   ├─ Process alternately, not simultaneously
   └─ Important for memory-constrained systems

3. DATA FORMAT CONVERSION
   ├─ Convert between formats
   ├─ Parse packed data
   └─ Handle variant records

4. OVERLAY STRUCTURES
   ├─ Map different record types
   ├─ Handle union types
   └─ Process different record formats
```

**Practical Example:**

```cobol
       01 RAW-BUFFER              PIC X(100).
       
       01 STRUCTURED-DATA REDEFINES RAW-BUFFER.
           05 RECORD-TYPE          PIC X(2).
           05 CUSTOMER-ID          PIC 9(7).
           05 TRANSACTION-DATE     PIC 9(8).
           05 AMOUNT               PIC 9(7)V99.
           05 FILLER               PIC X(73).
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       PROCESS-BUFFER.
           ACCEPT RAW-BUFFER FROM CONSOLE.
           
           *> Now access as STRUCTURED-DATA
           DISPLAY "Record Type: " RECORD-TYPE.
           DISPLAY "Customer: " CUSTOMER-ID.
           DISPLAY "Date: " TRANSACTION-DATE.
