## File Handling & I/O

### Q7: Explain the different file organizations and when to use each.

**Answer:**

```
FILE ORGANIZATIONS:

SEQUENTIAL:
├─ Records in physical order
├─ Read start to end
├─ Fast batch processing
├─ Cannot skip records
├─ Example: Transaction logs, backups
└─ When to use: Batch processes, archives

INDEXED (ISAM):
├─ Key-based access
├─ Fast random lookup
├─ Can also read sequentially
├─ One primary key, multiple alternate keys
├─ Example: Employee database, customer file
└─ When to use: Online lookups, mixed access

RELATIVE:
├─ Access by position/record number
├─ Less common
├─ Fixed record size
├─ Example: Fixed arrays, tables
└─ When to use: Fixed-size record files
```

**Code Examples:**

```cobol
       *> SEQUENTIAL FILE
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT TRANSACTION-FILE ASSIGN TO 'trans.dat'
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL.
       
       *> INDEXED FILE
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT EMPLOYEE-FILE ASSIGN TO 'emp.dat'
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               RECORD KEY IS EMPLOYEE-ID
               ALTERNATE RECORD KEY IS EMPLOYEE-SSN.
       
       *> RELATIVE FILE
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT RECORD-FILE ASSIGN TO 'records.dat'
               ORGANIZATION IS RELATIVE
               RELATIVE KEY IS RECORD-NUMBER.
```

**Access Patterns:**

```cobol
       SEQUENTIAL-READ.
           OPEN INPUT TRANSACTION-FILE.
           PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = 'Y'
               READ TRANSACTION-FILE
                   AT END
                       MOVE 'Y' TO WS-EOF
                   NOT AT END
                       PERFORM PROCESS
               END-READ
           END-PERFORM.
           CLOSE TRANSACTION-FILE.
       
       INDEXED-RANDOM-ACCESS.
           OPEN INPUT EMPLOYEE-FILE.
           MOVE 12345 TO EMPLOYEE-ID.
           
           READ EMPLOYEE-FILE
               INVALID KEY
                   DISPLAY "Not found"
               NOT INVALID KEY
                   DISPLAY "Found: " EMPLOYEE-NAME
           END-READ.
           CLOSE EMPLOYEE-FILE.
       
       INDEXED-SEQUENTIAL-ACCESS.
           OPEN INPUT EMPLOYEE-FILE.
           
           *> Start from key >= 50000
           START EMPLOYEE-FILE
               KEY IS >= EMPLOYEE-ID
           END-START.
           
           PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = 'Y'
               READ EMPLOYEE-FILE NEXT
                   AT END
                       MOVE 'Y' TO WS-EOF
                   NOT AT END
                       PERFORM PROCESS
               END-READ
           END-PERFORM.
           CLOSE EMPLOYEE-FILE.
```

**Performance Comparison:**

