### Q10: Explain PERFORM VARYING. How does it differ from simple PERFORM UNTIL?

**Answer:**

```
PERFORM UNTIL:
├─ Loops while condition is false
├─ Checks condition at start
├─ Manual counter increment
├─ Flexible conditions
└─ Use: General looping

PERFORM VARYING:
├─ Automatic counter increment
├─ Loop index management built-in
├─ Cleaner for array access
├─ More efficient
└─ Use: Array iteration, fixed loops
```

**Code Comparison:**

```cobol
       *> PERFORM UNTIL (Manual)
       PERFORM-UNTIL-APPROACH.
           MOVE 1 TO INDEX.
           PERFORM UNTIL INDEX > 100
               MOVE NUMBERS(INDEX) TO CURRENT-VALUE
               PERFORM PROCESS-VALUE
               ADD 1 TO INDEX
           END-PERFORM.
       
       *> PERFORM VARYING (Automatic)
       PERFORM-VARYING-APPROACH.
           PERFORM VARYING INDEX FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL INDEX > 100
               MOVE NUMBERS(INDEX) TO CURRENT-VALUE
               PERFORM PROCESS-VALUE
           END-PERFORM.
       
       *> PERFORM VARYING with nested loops
       PERFORM-NESTED-VARYING.
           PERFORM VARYING ROW FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL ROW > 10
               PERFORM VARYING COL FROM 1 BY 1
                   UNTIL COL > 10
                   MOVE (ROW, COL) TO MATRIX(ROW, COL)
               END-PERFORM
           END-PERFORM.
       
       *> PERFORM VARYING with custom step
       PERFORM-VARYING-STEP.
           PERFORM VARYING NUM FROM 1 BY 2
               UNTIL NUM > 100
               DISPLAY "Odd numbers: " NUM
           END-PERFORM.
           *> Displays: 1, 3, 5, 7, ... 99
       
       *> PERFORM VARYING with AFTER (nested)
       PERFORM-WITH-AFTER.
           PERFORM VARYING ROW FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL ROW > 5
               AFTER COL FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL COL > 10
               PERFORM PROCESS-CELL
           END-PERFORM.
```

**Performance Considerations:**

```
Method              Performance   Readability   Use Case
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PERFORM UNTIL       Good          Medium        Simple loops
PERFORM VARYING     Better        Good          Arrays
PERFORM N TIMES     Best          Good          Fixed loops
```

