### Q12: Explain LINKAGE SECTION. How do you pass data to subroutines?

**Answer:**

```cobol
       *> MAIN PROGRAM
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. MAIN-CALC.
       
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-INPUT-A              PIC 9(5) VALUE 10.
       01 WS-INPUT-B              PIC 9(5) VALUE 20.
       01 WS-RESULT               PIC 9(5).
       01 WS-STATUS               PIC 9.
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-LOGIC.
           *> Call subroutine
           CALL "MULTIPLY-CALC" USING BY VALUE WS-INPUT-A
               BY VALUE WS-INPUT-B
               BY REFERENCE WS-RESULT
               RETURNING WS-STATUS.
           
           DISPLAY "Result: " WS-RESULT.
           STOP RUN.
       
       
       *> SUBROUTINE PROGRAM
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. MULTIPLY-CALC.
       
       DATA DIVISION.
       LINKAGE SECTION.
       01 LS-PARAM-A              PIC 9(5).
       01 LS-PARAM-B              PIC 9(5).
       01 LS-RESULT               PIC 9(5).
       
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-TEMP                 PIC 9(9).
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LS-PARAM-A LS-PARAM-B
           LS-RESULT RETURNING WS-RETURN-CODE.
       
       MULTIPLY-LOGIC.
           COMPUTE WS-TEMP = LS-PARAM-A * LS-PARAM-B.
           
           IF WS-TEMP <= 99999
               MOVE WS-TEMP TO LS-RESULT
               MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
           ELSE
               MOVE 0 TO LS-RESULT
               MOVE 1 TO RETURN-CODE
           END-IF.
           
           GOBACK.
```

**Parameter Passing Methods:**

```
BY VALUE:
├─ Passes copy of data
├─ Subroutine cannot modify original
├─ Safer, but slower
└─ Use: Read-only parameters

BY REFERENCE:
├─ Passes memory address
├─ Subroutine CAN modify original
├─ Faster
└─ Use: Output parameters, arrays

RETURNING:
├─ Passes return value
├─ Single result value
├─ Clean semantics
└─ Use: Function-like returns
```

