## Database & SQL

### Q13: What is SQLCODE and how do you handle database errors?

**Answer:**

```cobol
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 SQLCODE              PIC S9(9) COMP.
       01 SQLERRMC             PIC X(70).
       01 SQL-ERROR-MESSAGE    PIC X(100).
       
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       
       SQL-OPERATION-WITH-ERROR-HANDLING.
           EXEC SQL
               SELECT SALARY INTO :EMP-SALARY
               FROM EMPLOYEES
               WHERE EMPLOYEE-ID = :EMP-ID
           END-EXEC.
           
           EVALUATE SQLCODE
               WHEN 0
                   DISPLAY "Success: Salary = " EMP-SALARY
               WHEN 100
                   MOVE "No employee found" 
                       TO SQL-ERROR-MESSAGE
               WHEN -803
                   MOVE "Duplicate key error" 
                       TO SQL-ERROR-MESSAGE
               WHEN -530
                   MOVE "Foreign key violation" 
                       TO SQL-ERROR-MESSAGE
               WHEN -911
                   MOVE "Deadlock or timeout" 
                       TO SQL-ERROR-MESSAGE
               WHEN -913
                   MOVE "Resource unavailable" 
                       TO SQL-ERROR-MESSAGE
               WHEN OTHER
                   STRING
                       "Database error: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
                       SQLCODE DELIMITED BY SIZE
                       " - " DELIMITED BY SIZE
                       SQLERRMC DELIMITED BY SIZE
                       INTO SQL-ERROR-MESSAGE
                   END-STRING
           END-EVALUATE.
           
           IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
               PERFORM HANDLE-SQL-ERROR
           END-IF.
       
       HANDLE-SQL-ERROR.
           DISPLAY SQL-ERROR-MESSAGE.
           
           EVALUATE SQLCODE
               WHEN -911
                   *> Retry logic for deadlock
                   PERFORM RETRY-OPERATION
               WHEN 100
                   *> No data found - may not be error
                   CONTINUE
               WHEN OTHER
                   *> Other errors - cleanup and exit
                   PERFORM CLEANUP
                   GOBACK
           END-EVALUATE.
       
       RETRY-OPERATION.
           MOVE 0 TO RETRY-COUNT.
           PERFORM UNTIL RETRY-COUNT > 3
               ADD 1 TO RETRY-COUNT
               ACCEPT WS-DELAY FROM TIME
               *> Retry SQL operation
               EXIT PERFORM
           END-PERFORM.
       
       TRANSACTION-WITH-ROLLBACK.
           EXEC SQL BEGIN WORK END-EXEC.
           
           PERFORM INSERT-NEW-RECORD.
           IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
               EXEC SQL ROLLBACK WORK END-EXEC
               DISPLAY "Insert failed - rolled back"
               GOBACK
           END-IF.
           
           PERFORM UPDATE-EXISTING.
           IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
               EXEC SQL ROLLBACK WORK END-EXEC
               DISPLAY "Update failed - rolled back"
               GOBACK
           END-IF.
           
           EXEC SQL COMMIT WORK END-EXEC.
           DISPLAY "Transaction committed successfully".
```

**SQLCODE Reference:**

```
Value   Meaning
─────────────────────────────────────────
0       Successful execution
+100    No more data (NOT an error)
-1      Rollback
-803    Duplicate key value
-530    Foreign key constraint violation
-911    Deadlock or resource timeout
-913    Resource unavailable
-917    Binding error
-922    Unknown statement type
-1003   Undefined table/view
```

