## Performance & Optimization

### Q15: How can you optimize COBOL programs for performance?

**Answer:**

```
OPTIMIZATION TECHNIQUES:

1. DATA STORAGE
   ├─ Use COMP/COMP-3 for frequently used numbers
   ├─ Avoid unnecessary REDEFINES
   ├─ Use appropriate field sizes
   └─ Result: 30-50% space reduction

2. FILE ACCESS
   ├─ Use indexed files for random access
   ├─ Batch sequential reads
   ├─ Avoid unnecessary file opens/closes
   └─ Result: 10x faster lookups

3. CALCULATIONS
   ├─ Use INTEGER division when appropriate
   ├─ Pre-calculate constants
   ├─ Avoid repeated calculations in loops
   └─ Result: 2-3x faster math

4. PROGRAM STRUCTURE
   ├─ Minimize nested loops
   ├─ Use PERFORM VARYING instead of PERFORM UNTIL
   ├─ Avoid deep paragraph nesting
   └─ Result: 5-10% improvement

5. I/O BUFFERING
   ├─ Use buffering for multiple reads
   ├─ Minimize file access
   ├─ Batch operations
   └─ Result: Significant I/O reduction
```

**Code Examples:**

```cobol
       *> OPTIMIZATION 1: Use COMP types
       
       *> BEFORE (Slow)
       01 COUNTER              PIC 9(6).           *> 6 bytes
       01 AMOUNT               PIC 9(7)V99.        *> 5 bytes
       
       *> AFTER (Fast)
       01 COUNTER              PIC 9(6) COMP.      *> 2-3 bytes
       01 AMOUNT               PIC 9(7)V99 COMP-3. *> 3 bytes
       
       
       *> OPTIMIZATION 2: File access patterns
       
       *> BEFORE (Slow - sequential search)
       SLOW-LOOKUP.
           OPEN INPUT CUSTOMER-FILE.
           PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = 'Y'
               READ CUSTOMER-FILE
                   AT END MOVE 'Y' TO WS-EOF
                   NOT AT END
                       IF CUSTOMER-ID = SEARCH-ID
                           MOVE CUSTOMER-NAME TO RESULT
                           MOVE 'Y' TO WS-EOF
                       END-IF
               END-READ
           END-PERFORM.
       
       *> AFTER (Fast - indexed access)
       FAST-LOOKUP.
           OPEN INPUT CUSTOMER-FILE.
           READ CUSTOMER-FILE
               INVALID KEY
                   MOVE SPACES TO RESULT
               NOT INVALID KEY
                   MOVE CUSTOMER-NAME TO RESULT
           END-READ.
           CLOSE CUSTOMER-FILE.
       
       
       *> OPTIMIZATION 3: Loop efficiency
       
       *> BEFORE (Slower)
       SLOWER-LOOP.
           MOVE 1 TO INDEX.
           PERFORM UNTIL INDEX > 1000
               COMPUTE SQUARE = INDEX * INDEX
               COMPUTE CUBE = INDEX * INDEX * INDEX
               ADD 1 TO INDEX
           END-PERFORM.
       
       *> AFTER (Faster)
       FASTER-LOOP.
           PERFORM VARYING INDEX FROM 1 BY 1
               UNTIL INDEX > 1000
               COMPUTE SQUARE = INDEX * INDEX
               COMPUTE CUBE = INDEX * SQUARE
           END-PERFORM.
```

